description:
WHAT: Every editor prompt pays full MCP cold start before the first model request: process spawn + initialize + tools/list for node/python servers is typically 300 ms to 3 s per server, and the end-of-turn shutdown adds the graceful drain. With several servers this dominates ACP time-to-first-token and burns CPU/RAM relaunching servers that the TUI path keeps warm. Deferred (mcp_search) discovery sessions are also re-captured per prompt (context.mcp_discovery).

WHERE (main at b56d7a74): src/extras/acp/mod.rs:3275-3276; src/extras/acp/mod.rs:4064-4084; src/extras/acp/mod.rs:3329-3332; src/extras/acp/mod.rs:4212-4232; src/startup.rs:509-523; src/extras/mcp/mod.rs:253-358

HOT PATH: handle_prompt -> spawn_turn -> run_prompt -> execute_prompt -> connect_prompt_mcp -> startup::connect_headless_mcp -> McpClientManager::connect_config_in_binding (spawn every stdio server + initialize handshake, HTTP: TCP/TLS + OAuth restore, up to MCP_INITIALIZE_TIMEOUT=10 s each, 8-way concurrent) -> build_agent_in_workspace -> collect_tools_with_timeouts (tools/list to every server, OnceCell is per handle and handles are new) -> spawn_auxiliary_discovery (prompts/resources list) -> after the turn run_prompt awaits manager.shutdown() (graceful wait up to 3 s per server). Once per ACP session/prompt, including every /cron fire; the TUI keeps one manager for the whole session (ui::rebind_mcp_manager only on worktree/config changes).

