HOW: Make the McpClientManager session-scoped: store it (Arc) in SessionState next to read_tracker/todo_store, connect it lazily on the first tool-enabled prompt of a session (or on session/new), reuse it for later prompts, and close it in handle_close_session / connection teardown. Per-call staleness is already guarded by ServerSourceProof::is_current and client_is_live, so reuse does not weaken the source-currency contract; keep the work_scope cancellation wiring by connecting inside a session-owned scope.

VERIFY: Add an ACP protocol test that runs two session/prompt turns in one session against a stdio fixture server and asserts a single spawn (count initialize requests in the fixture); update mcp_stdio_teardown_precedes_terminal_response_and_session_settlement (src/extras/acp/mod.rs:8880) to expect teardown at session close instead of per prompt; measure second-prompt time-to-first-notification before/after with one configured npx server.

