WHAT: prepare() runs entirely synchronously inside the tool's async fn: it captures a brand-new WorkspaceBinding for the checkpoint directory (canonicalize + cap_std open + two fstat + validate_private_root twice), rescans every existing checkpoint blob (symlink_metadata + open + validate_private_file + metadata, up to MAX_RECORDS=512 blobs, i.e. ~2000 syscalls late in a session) even though state.data.blobs already tracks them, then writes the preimage with the durable variant: temp.sync_all() and sync_directory() (std's sync_all is fcntl(F_FULLFSYNC) on macOS, typically 10-50 ms each on Apple SSDs). That is tens of ms of blocking work per edit on a 4-worker runtime shared with the TUI event loop, before the edit's own publish happens. cttyn.60 fixed the same pattern for session save but not for checkpoints.

