pub fn migrate_legacy_path(
    request: &LegacyMigrationRequest,
) -> Result<LegacyMigrationStatus, LegacyMigrationError> {
    if path_exists_no_follow(&request.canonical, request.artifact, request.kind)? {
        if !path_exists_no_follow(&request.marker, request.artifact, LegacyArtifactKind::File)? {
            let canonical_identity = content_identity(&request.canonical).map_err(|source| {
                LegacyMigrationError::Io { artifact: request.artifact, path: request.canonical.clone(), source }
            })?;
            for candidate in
                existing_candidates(&request.candidates, request.artifact, request.kind)?
            {
                let candidate_identity = content_identity(&candidate)...;
                if candidate_identity == canonical_identity {
                    write_migration_marker(request, &candidate, &canonical_identity)?;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
        return Ok(LegacyMigrationStatus::CanonicalPresent);
    }
// content_identity(): recursive read_dir + full file read into Sha256 for every entry (paths.rs:2861-2909)
```

HOW: In migrate_legacy_path, enumerate existing_candidates first and return CanonicalPresent immediately when it is empty (no hashing). When candidates exist but none match, still write a marker (e.g. with content_sha256 = "" / a 'no-legacy-source' field) so the comparison is never repeated. Alternatively hash only when the candidate metadata (size/mtime) could possibly match. Consider moving the whole convergence off the main thread or behind a once-per-version marker file.

VERIFY: Existing tests legacy_path_migration_is_verified_idempotent_and_retains_source / legacy_path_migration_repairs_marker_after_publish_interruption / legacy_path_migration_never_chooses_differing_candidates must stay green. Add a test: canonical sessions dir with a large fake file and no candidates -> migrate_legacy_path must not open the file (use a FIFO or count opens via a probe); measure `time mini-agent --print-config` before/after with a populated state/sessions dir.

