WHAT: scan_with reads the entire append-only ledger (bounded only at 64 MiB / 65 536 rows), serde-parses every row, validates it, re-serializes it with serde_json::to_vec and SHA-256s it to build a BTreeMap<Uuid,[u8;32]> of identities - solely to detect a duplicate id for the 1-3 rows being appended. On top of that each flush does ~5 revalidate() passes (each: canonicalize + 2 stat + open a second fd + 2 fstat) plus a file.sync_all(). The cost is O(total rows ever recorded across all sessions) per model call and grows for the lifetime of the install: at the 65k-row cap this is tens of MB of JSON parse + hash per tool round. The 2026-10-15 fix (cttyn.63) added a checkpoint for the startup session_summary scan only; the per-flush ScanMode::Flush scan was left as a full scan.

