WHAT: Each visited entry costs openat + fstat + close (3 syscalls) plus two PathBuf joins, regardless of whether the pattern, include glob, skip-dir, ignore chain or deny filter would discard it. A `find_files **/*.rs` or `grep include:*.rs` over a 50k-entry tree therefore performs ~150k syscalls and opens 45k irrelevant files; ripgrep/ignore avoid this by using readdir's d_type and only opening files that pass the filters. The open of a FIFO/device is also avoided only by O_NONBLOCK. The macOS/Linux DirectoryEntry structs already carry file_type but DirectoryReader drops it.

