Diagnosis of the opacity, from the cited artefacts.

The exact line in job 102517117403 is:

  Windows AppContainer sandbox probe failed: cached production AppContainer preflight failed

It ends at "failed" with no trailing colon, which is the tell: it cannot have come from a format that appends a cause. At b5327ff the probe read:

  if !is_available() || !is_available() {
      return Err("cached production AppContainer preflight failed".into());
  }

is_available() returns a bool, so the underlying Result from the cached preflight was reduced to a yes/no and the cause was discarded before the error was ever constructed. That is the whole explanation for "No failed Rust assertion or underlying preflight diagnostic was emitted" -- nothing was suppressed downstream, the cause was destroyed at the source. The outer eprintln in maybe_run_from_args (src/sandbox/windows.rs, PROBE_ARG arm) then printed exactly the string it was given.

Consequence for this bead: the cause of THAT run is not recoverable from the logs, by construction. No amount of re-reading job 102517117403 will produce it, and it should not be inferred.

